# tests/manifest -- one line per case. Columns 1-4 are fixed; the rest are key=value metadata.
#
#   <name>  <mode>  <tier>  <timeout>  [key=value ...]
#
# name     unique case id, also the display name
# mode     which tests/lib/modes/<mode>.sh runs it -- the only place a run method is named
# tier     fast | smoke | gate | manual   (fast < smoke < gate; manual only when named)
# timeout  seconds, applied by the harness to each product invocation
# fields   mode metadata; the runner refuses a field the mode does not declare
#
# Values cannot contain spaces: write %20. {DATA} is the data root, {ROOT} the repository root.
# A needs= path that is absent makes the case SKIP, never FAIL.
#
# Case owners: corpus and project rows come from the corpus batch; programs/ holds every guest
# program; fixtures/ the crates and data a mode needs.

# Corpus batch: one line per real-crate driver. tier: smoke runs daily, gate is the full
# defense line, manual only when named. group= is the budget key (heavy entries stack with
# --group). needs= absent makes the case SKIP. verdict=oracle:<name> compares stdout with
# data/fixtures/oracles/<name>.txt; xfail=<code>:<pattern> registers a known red.
